From a71d8fa05e6acb2620ede4a3f41947a607130a12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phillippe Pelzer <phil.pelzer@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 15:09:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(dvd): add dvdread:// input protocol alongside the
 dvdvideo demuxer

Add a thin URLProtocol over libdvdread that exposes a title set's VOBs
as a seekable MPEG-PS byte stream, restoring scheme://device URI
symmetry with bluray:// (closes #27).

- libavformat/dvdread_proto.c modeled on bluray.c: accepts
  dvdread:PATH, dvdread://PATH and dvdread:///ABS/PATH; -title N
  selects a logical title (resolved to its VTS via the VMG IFO),
  default auto-picks the largest title set (main feature); unaligned
  reads served through a single-block cache, aligned spans go straight
  to DVDReadBlocks
- scripts/58-dvdread-protocol.sh registers the protocol via three
  anchored, idempotent edits (protocols.c extern, Makefile object,
  dvdread_protocol_deps in configure); protocol auto-enables since the
  build already passes --enable-libdvdread; skips when libdvdread is
  absent
- document the protocol in the README component table

Verified against FFmpeg 8.1.2: protocol stream is byte-identical to
the raw title VOBs (including odd-offset seeks), stock-vs-patched
builds differ by exactly the added protocol, and dvdvideo demuxer
input is unaffected.


